From 0296ca0c0112ede12010d66f251e2ef72990207a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Data-crea <sattler.daniel@hotmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 05:38:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] OrionLayer Open Fix 125: MSG_CANCEL_FIELD holds the real
 mouse off like the two injected clicks (it pushed a right click without
 setting g_injected_mouse_pending, so the physical mouse could rewrite its
 release, the defect open fix 3 describes)

OrionLayer, open fix 125.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/ext/ext_api.cpp | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/ext/ext_api.cpp b/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
index 019b6edb..1db1463e 100644
--- a/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
+++ b/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
@@ -3954,6 +3954,11 @@ static void ProcessInput() {
                 // The field rect is in game space, so this centre
                 // needs the same conversion as an injected click —
                 // it is the same defect reached by a different door.
+                // OrionLayer, open fix 125. The same hold on the real
+                // mouse as the other two injections (INJECT_CLICK,
+                // INJECT_RIGHT_CLICK): without it the physical mouse
+                // rewrote this right click's release (open fix 3).
+                g_injected_mouse_pending = true;
                 float cx = 0.0f;
                 float cy = 0.0f;
                 Game_Point_To_Window_Point_(
